In Python, getters and setters are used to control access to class variables.
They are commonly implemented using the @property decorator.

🔹 Why use Getters & Setters?
✔ Encapsulation (data hiding)
✔ Validation before setting values
✔ Read-only or controlled access
✔ Cleaner & safer code
🔹 Basic Example (Without Property – NOT recommended)
class Person:
    def __init__(self, age):
        self.age = age
❌ Problem: Anyone can set invalid values
p = Person(-5)
✅ Correct Way: Using @property (Recommended)
Getter & Setter Example
class Person:
    def __init__(self, age):
        self._age = age   # protected variable

    @property
    def age(self):
        return self._age

    @age.setter
    def age(self, value):
        if value < 0:
            print("Age cannot be negative")
        else:
            self._age = value
Usage:
p = Person(25)
print(p.age)     # getter

p.age = 30       # setter
print(p.age)

p.age = -10      # invalid
📌 Output:
25
30
Age cannot be negative
🔹 How it Works (Important)
p.age        → calls age() getter  
p.age = 30   → calls age(value) setter
Looks like variable access but works like methods 🔥
🔹 Read-Only Property (Only Getter)
class Product:
    def __init__(self, price):
        self._price = price

    @property
    def price(self):
        return self._price
p = Product(100)
print(p.price)
p.price = 200  # ❌ Error (no setter)
🔹 Write-Only Property (Rare)
class Secret:
    def __init__(self):
        self._data = None

    def set_data(self, value):
        self._data = value

    data = property(fset=set_data)
🔹 Getter & Setter Without @property (Old Style)
class Demo:
    def get_x(self):
        return self._x

    def set_x(self, value):
        self._x = value

    x = property(get_x, set_x)
🔹 Real-Life Example (Bank Account)
class BankAccount:
    def __init__(self, balance):
        self._balance = balance

    @property
    def balance(self):
        return self._balance

    @balance.setter
    def balance(self, amount):
        if amount < 0:
            print("Invalid balance")
        else:
            self._balance = amount
            
🔹 Getters & Setters vs Direct Access
Direct Variable	Getter & Setter
No validation	Validation allowed
Less secure	Encapsulation
Easy but unsafe	Professional approach


